From 762b21c81b7367b223a3e82b5f927ec0fd4e4a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MeshCrowd measurement kit <meter@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:35:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add cost and usability measurement kit under
 evaluation/meter

- probes (battery, scan cadence, storage/traffic) as classes the campaign build can compile,
  plus MeshCrowdMeterHooks.kt with the call sites in MeshCrowdEvaluationHooks style
- meter-app: standalone foreground-service APK reproducing the sensing duty cycle
  (15 s epoch, 5 bursts/30 s); scripts/build_apk_local.sh builds it with kotlinc+d8+aapt2 only
- run_leg.sh / storage_net_snapshot.sh capture protocol; parse_leg.py + meter_report.py +
  storage_delta.py + usability_report.py turn captures into LaTeX and paste-ready prose,
  reporting n/m rather than zero whenever a capture did not yield a quantity
- protocol.md (legs B1-B6, tasks U1-U8, Wilson intervals, pilot caveat), consent form,
  leg worksheet, latex/measurement_tables.tex skeleton
- tests/: synthetic fixture + 30 assertions over the analysers (labelled synthetic, not data)
- session.schema.json gains an optional 'cost' object; manifest fragment notes that the
  probes need no new permission; sync_probes.sh guards the two probe copies against drift
